# BoxOps {{version}}

The release build of [BoxOps](https://github.com/Allenfp/BoxOps) {{version}}
(build `{{build}}`), made by its release workflow from commit
[`{{sourceShort}}`](https://github.com/Allenfp/BoxOps/tree/{{source}}) of
BoxOps' source. The source, the docs and the issues are on BoxOps' `main`
branch; this commit, on its `releases` branch, holds the built release only.

A roadmap repository (one made from
[the starter](https://github.com/Allenfp/boxops-starter)) runs this commit,
pinned by its SHA in its workflows:
`uses: Allenfp/BoxOps@<this commit's SHA> # v{{version}}`.

- `action.yml` and `dist/action.mjs`: the GitHub Action. It checks the
  roadmap and assembles the Pages site, reading git objects only: no
  network, no token, no build.
- `dist/boxops.mjs`: the engine and the command-line tool, unminified. A
  roadmap repository's launcher, `node .boxops/boxops.mjs`, runs it.
- `dist/app/`: the app, built.
- `BUILD.json`: the build, its data format and contract numbers, and every
  other file's SHA-256.
- `LICENSE`: BoxOps' licence (MIT). `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`: those of the
  packages `dist/boxops.mjs` bundles. `dist/app/licenses.txt`: those of what
  the app bundles, and of its icons.

To check that a file came from BoxOps' release workflow:

```sh
gh attestation verify <file> -R Allenfp/BoxOps --signer-workflow Allenfp/BoxOps/.github/workflows/release.yml
```
